    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d863">

                <pb facs="0863" n="859" xml:id="pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.002/917: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dooman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-09-02T12:00:00+09:00">September 2,
                            1939—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received September 2—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>451. Department’s 183, August 30, 6 p.m., to Peiping. I delivered yesterday at
                    the Foreign Office a first person note<anchor n="11" xml:id="d863-f1"/>
                    protesting against seizure and occupation of Swatow Customs. Having done so, I
                    invited the British and French Ambassadors to take similar action. They are
                    consulting their respective Governments.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Peiping. Peiping please repeat to Chungking and Swatow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dooman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
